// driver_sqlite.go — SQLite backend (B-mod-sqlite-pg-bidi v1.5.4).
//
// Sister file to driver_postgres.go. The PG migration set has been
// the canonical one since v1.3.0 (B-mod-db-retry); B-mod-sqlite-pg-bidi
// restores explicit SQLite support by running the same migration
// numbers through the SQLite migration functions in
// migrations_sqlite.go (generated by scripts/port_migrations_sqlite.py
// via reverse-substitution from the PG source).
//
// Why a separate file (not just shadow-files):
//
// The PG and SQLite migration SETS have parallel structure (same
// version numbers, same metadata) but the DDL is dialect-specific
// (BIGSERIAL vs INTEGER PK AUTOINCREMENT, EXTRACT(EPOCH) vs
// strftime('%s'), INSERT OR IGNORE vs ON CONFLICT, etc.). Putting
// the registry + Run loop in the same file as the migration
// functions would couple them too tightly. The PG side stays in
// driver_postgres.go (existing); the SQLite side gets a parallel
// driver_sqlite.go that mirrors the structure.
//
// sqliteMigrations mirrors pgMigrations: same version numbers, same
// Name strings, same SourceFile pointers (so the B198 audit
// `applied_migrations.source_file` column shows the same Go file
// regardless of which DB applied the migration — the migration
// AUTHORSHIP is shared, only the DDL differs).
package db

import (
	"database/sql"
	"fmt"
	"log"
)

